  "result": "Perfect! All 381 tests pass (15 new tests added for the dashboard function).\n\n**Dashboard implementation complete:**\n\n1. **Added `dashboard(invoices, asOf)` to `src/reports.js`** that returns:\n   - **counts**: Number of invoices per status (draft, issued, partially_paid, paid)\n   - **outstanding**: Total amount still due on invoices with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n   - **overdue**: Object with count and total amount of invoices past due date\n   - **topCustomers**: Array of top 3 customers by outstanding balance (highest first), as `[{ customerId, due }, ...]`\n\n2. **Key features**:\n   - Aggregates multiple invoices per customer\n   - Excludes paid invoices from outstanding and top customers\n   - Only includes customers with balance > 0 in top customers\n   - Handles partially paid invoices (includes remaining balance)\n   - Uses existing `overdueInvoices()` function for overdue data\n   - Returns error for invalid dates\n\n3. **Added 15 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - Invalid date validation\n   - Empty invoice list\n   - Status counting accuracy\n   - Outstanding amount calculation\n   - Overdue tracking (count and amount)\n   - Top customers sorted by amount due\n   - Top customers limited to 3\n   - Multi-invoice aggregation per customer\n   - Exclusion of paid invoices\n   - Exclusion of zero-balance customers\n   - Partially paid invoice handling\n   - Draft invoice handling\n   - Mixed invoice statuses",
